fact WorkItem(id: "WI-422", description: some(value: "Loader/resolution: a selectively-imported operation referenced by BARE short name resolves AMBIGUOUSLY inside a sort scope that has `requires Spec[T]`. Surfaced (not caused) by WI-421. SYMPTOM: with `import anthill.prelude.List.{member}`, a bare `member` reference inside `sort Box requires Eq[T]` emits `warning: ambiguous symbol 'member' ... candidates [member, anthill.prelude.List.member]`; remap_symbol's Ambiguous arm (load.rs ~4405) then interns a FRESH unresolved symbol, so the bare reference cascades into a hard `expected resolved name, got unresolved` / `unknown functor` failure downstream. AmbiguousSymbol is itself non-load-blocking (load.rs is_load_blocking) but the cascade is fatal on the bare path. TRIGGER (narrowed empirically via minimal probes -- each toggle independently makes it CLEAN): the warning fires ONLY when ALL of (1) the enclosing sort declares `requires Spec[T]`, (2) the op is referenced by bare selectively-imported short name (not a qualified dot form), and (3) the reference is in a NESTED scope (sort/op body), not namespace level. Removing the `requires`, qualifying the ref as `List.member`, OR moving the ref to namespace level each independently removes the ambiguity. So a requires-induced parent-scope linkage re-surfaces a SECOND reachable `member` during the nested parent-walk (intern.rs resolve_in_scope_recursive ~300-352, which collects matches across eligible parents and reports >1 distinct symbol as Ambiguous). The bare candidate renders as `member` (candidate_names returns the bare `name` for an Unresolved symbol, qualified_name for a Resolved one); its exact identity is NOT yet root-caused (needs a debug build) -- candidates to check: List's companion `rule member` head functor, Set.member, or a globally-interned `member` key. INVESTIGATE that first. IMPACT: a user following the obvious `import List.{member}` pattern inside a requires-bearing sort hits a confusing ambiguity + failure with a non-obvious fix. WORKAROUND (the WI-421 a2 blessed idiom, already pinned by wi421_abstract_requires_op_via_lambda_idiom_evals in eval_test.rs): use the qualified dot form `List.member(...)`, wrapped in a lambda for HOF use, with NO `member` import -- loads warning-clean. NOT a blocker for WI-421 (closed via a2). FIX DIRECTION: a selective-import alias resolvable in an ancestor scope should take precedence over (or dedupe against) a symbol re-surfaced only via the requires-induced scope linkage, so a bare selectively-imported name resolves unambiguously inside a requires-bearing nested scope. ACCEPTANCE: `sort Box requires Eq[T]` with `import anthill.prelude.List.{member}` can reference bare `member` inside an op body without an ambiguity warning or an unresolved failure (resolving to List.member); a regression test pins it; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-07T16:45:54Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-422", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED 2026-06-07 (65da79b, rebased onto WI-068 Int->Int64; green 1556). Root cause was NOT yet-root-caused at file time: the phantom 'member' candidate is the loader-internal reflection FACT FUNCTOR 'member' (emits member(name,kind,parent) facts), registered as a degenerate-qualified GLOBAL LOCAL via define(). 'requires Eq[T]' opens Box->Eq->prelude->_global, bypassing the namespace's member->List.member import alias and resurfacing the global member as a rival. Fix: new SymbolTable::define_qualified_only (by_qualified_name only, never in any scope locals); the 3 kernel fact-functors (member/meta/SortAlias) moved to it; member additionally got the proper name anthill.reflect.member (user steer: 'if we emit in db member, do it as a fully qualified name'). Consumers query member facts by SORT (Member) + positional args, never the functor symbol, so the rename is transparent (make_name_term interns, doesn't scope-resolve). /code-review max-effort (2 finders + sweep): 0 bugs; one reverted the fix and confirmed the test fails with the exact cascade. ALTITUDE FINDING (both reviewers, NOT WI-422 scope, NOT fixed): KERNEL_META_SORTS (Sort/Entity/Fact/Rule/Operation/Namespace/Requirement/Description/Constraint/Member) remain bare GLOBAL LOCALS via define() with the structurally-identical leak — a user-defined sort whose name collides with a kernel meta-sort, selectively imported into a requires-bearing sort, hits the same ambiguity. Lower-risk (PascalCase kernel names rarely user-shadowed; trigger more contrived than the real List.member case) and possibly user/reflection-facing (delocalizing needs verifying no legit bare scope-ref; fact indexing is safe since make_name_term interns). Two closes: (a) delocalize the meta-sorts too, or (b) the DEEPER fix — make resolve_in_scope_recursive prefer a nearer/import-alias match over a requires-reached global local (changes the general 'collect-all-then-flag-ambiguous' policy). Candidate follow-up WI pending user decision.", at: "2026-06-07T16:46:21Z")
